Z||000000||Gottico||11-07-2000||12:28 AM||||Ok 88’ Formula 5spd, Took it for a drive today to figure out what exactly is the problem. Engine runs fine at any and all RPM’s accept when in gear. Today it is accelerating with some serious vibration (more than normal). Came home and found a broken transmission mount. Replaced that and now the acceleration problem is back, can’t get over 1500 rpm’s without bad vibration and backfiring. Trans fluid looks good. The only other thing I noticed is that the tach is jumpy but I think that’s just the tach filter…<BR>Thanx for all the replies on the first one… Checked codes, nothing. Coolant sensor was replaced last month. Tune up done about the sametime. Clutch is about six months old. Leaking clutch master cylinder but has pressure. Any other ideas before I cut the converter off???? <P>||||reg||9
Z||000001||StuGood||11-07-2000||12:54 AM||||The tach filter can mess up the ignition's performance.  Unplug tach filter and see if the other problems go away (zero-cost test).  If so, replace the tach filter.<P>Apologize if you already knew this.   <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 11-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gottico||11-07-2000||12:58 AM||||Nope... didn't know that... I'll try that...||||reg||1
